WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
28 January 1948.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.170
On BBC radio, two philosophers
sit down to argue about God.

3
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.990
Frederick Copleston is a Jesuit priest.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.660
Bertrand Russell calls
himself an agnostic,

5
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.100
not an atheist.

6
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.340
Copleston starts with himself.

7
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.370
He exists only because of
his parents, air and food.

8
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.940
So does the universe as a
whole need an explanation too,

9
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.100
or is it simply there?

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.040
In this mission, you'll build
Copleston's argument from contingency,

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.500
step by step.

12
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.450
Then you'll hear Russell's replies, and
their clash over religious experience.

13
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: weigh up whether
the universe needs an explanation,

14
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.760
or is simply there.
